  "verdict": "On MERRA-2 air the capsule's deep edge (isolated, Brutsaert's clear sky, no sun, still air) bottoms at −39.02 °C over 2001–2020 and stays above the capsule requirement of −40 °C; under the product's clear-sky flux the same lump on the same air bottoms at −36.01 °C, on ERA5 air under the formula at −33.45 °C. Below the EDLC floor of −25 °C: 1059 hours (formula sky), 660 (product's clear sky), 399 (ERA5 air, formula sky). Solved under the formula sky at the minimum of each of the 3653 days before the hourly record, the lump is below the requirement on 2 (1997-12-16, 1997-12-17), by at most 1.17 K; with the product's clear-sky ratios, or with a tenth of the daily-mean wind, the lump there is above the requirement. With `71`'s ×0.7 reading of the still-air kernel the formula-sky run on MERRA-2 air bottoms at −40.21 °C with 3 hours below the requirement inside the hourly record, the product's clear-sky run at −36.55 °C."
